{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-5b558ac8", "text": "A time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones together; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 3:5", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-16a92bd6", "text": "Yea, though he live a thousand years twice told , yet hath he seen no good: do not all go to one place?", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 6:6", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-e015430e", "text": "If the iron be blunt, and he do not whet the edge, then must he put to more strength: but wisdom is profitable to direct.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 10:10", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-8f4aec23", "text": "Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher, vanity of vanities; all is vanity.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:2", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 12, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-1c64afed", "text": "What profit hath a man of all his labour which he taketh under the sun?", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:3", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 15, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-d893156c", "text": "One generation passeth away, and another generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:4", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 14, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-b2e8fc7b", "text": "The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:5", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 17, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-147de5e8", "text": "The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to his circuits.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:6", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-9d8c396a", "text": "All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea is not full; unto the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:7", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-b540e66e", "text": "All things are full of labour; man cannot utter it: the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:8", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-354bb41a", "text": "The thing that hath been, it is that which shall be; and that which is done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:9", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 31, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-b60407cd", "text": "Is there any thing whereof it may be said, See, this is new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:10", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-ef9d2bb4", "text": "There is no remembrance of former things; neither shall there be any remembrance of things that are to come with those that shall come after.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 1:11", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "kjv-84bc8ca3", "text": "I said in mine heart, Go to now, I will prove thee with mirth, therefore enjoy pleasure: and, behold, this also is vanity.", "role": "qoheleth", "origin": "kjv", "book": "Ecclesiastes", "ref": "Ecc 2:1", "tone": "neutral", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "KJV public domain (US)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "hopeful", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh', 'neutral'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
